4989 channa ¹ 'covered' MBh. [√ chad ¹] Pa. channa - 'covered, thatched', n. 'secret place';
Pk. chaṇṇa - 'covered'; S. chano m. 'shed', Ku. chāno ;
N. chānu 'roof'; A. sāniba 'to cover, spread, fill';
OMarw. chānaü 'hidden'; OG. chānaüṁ 'secretly', G. chānũ 'hidden, secret'; Si. san 'covered', sb. 'hiding', han , an 'dressed' (pp. of han̆dinavā < chandáyati ¹). * channi-; *channapradēśa -. Addenda: channa-¹: S.kcch. chano m. 'temporary residence for
a marriage party during a wedding'; Garh. chān 'cowshed'; A. spel. chāniba 'to cover' AFD 337.

